From: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 23:30:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_eth_soc: enable RSS on MT7987

MT7987 has the same four PDMA RX rings and interrupts as MT7988.  Use them
for RSS, so that received traffic is spread over four rings and CPUs
instead of one.  The device tree provides the interrupts as pdma0 to
pdma3; without them the driver keeps one RX ring.

Based-on-patch-by: Mason Chang <mason-cw.chang@mediatek.com>
Link: https://github.com/mediatek/mtk-openwrt-feeds/blob/22213a321b6dafb2a5e01def97363420e6e938fd/25.12/files/target/linux/mediatek/patches-6.12/999-eth-09-mtk_eth_soc-add-rss-support.patch
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -6866,6 +6866,7 @@ static const struct mtk_soc_data mt7986_
 static const struct mtk_soc_data mt7987_data = {
 	.reg_map = &mt7988_reg_map,
 	.ana_rgc3 = 0x128,
+	.rss_num = 4,
 	.caps = MT7987_CAPS,
 	.hw_features = MTK_HW_FEATURES,
 	.required_clks = MT7987_CLKS_BITMAP,
